{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910997-drones-and-demons","id":910997,"title":"Drones and Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-09T11:50:07-07:00","id":910997,"title":"Drones and Demons","content":"Ok so a few demon players want to use drones to do stuff.<br /> <br /> It got me thinking could demons create drones calling them imps (intelligent manipulation programs) if they wanted with limited intelligence to do things. They could use a drone to follow and watch people, Having them explode to take things out or even using them to hack into stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about using the gadget creation rules but I'm looking for advice on this idea. So if anyone has any other ideas on this I would love to hear it because right now this is just a seed of an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:57:55-07:00","id":911123,"title":"","content":"They could be Cryptids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:19:13-07:00","id":911461,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Ephsy. The rules for cryptids may be the easiest to adapt to this. I may suggest to use birds as the base animal for the mechanics even if that isn't the true origin of the being.<br /> <br /> An alternative if these will be mundane would be to use crafts rolls to make the drone, computer rolls to program and operate. If they want it to have A.I. possibly have them throw a spirit into it or have them design the A.I. with the required successes related to what mental harry they want. Or for a simpler way to establish the dice pool have it set up as a retainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:14:08-07:00","id":911921,"title":"","content":"Using the Exploit Hellhound on some trained birds seems like a perfectly viable solution .<br /> <br /> In my campaign the players once used Download Knowledge + Animate to create a Gadget out of a corpse, which they used as a chauffeur. In general Near-Field effects combined with Lambda gadgets gives almost unlimited license to create any effect you might be looking for, including animate servants.<br /> <br /> If you're not opposed to using real drones (civilian or military) in the campaign, a character with a few dots in craft(electonics) can build there own with a trip to Radioshack.<br /> <br /> The players could subvert an appropriate Defense Infrastructure. The local Lockheed Martin factory could very well be a G-M facility, and the drones could be the Output.<br /> <br /> Finally, if the drones operators are sleepers, and the players find a way to suborn the sleeper's programing, the difference can be academic .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:22:41-07:00","id":911983,"title":"","content":"One could always use some sort of Terrible Avatar Gadget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}